hadiths[201]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6009","Safwan ibn Umayyah (رضي الله عنه) reported: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Urfutah ibn Nuhayk al-Tamimi stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, I and my household earn our provision from this hunting, and we have therein a share and blessing, yet it preoccupies us from remembrance of Allah and from prayer in congregation, and we have need of it — do you declare it lawful or unlawful? > **""I declare it lawful, for Allah Almighty has made it lawful. What an excellent occupation. Allah is most entitled to accept excuse. Before me were Messengers of Allah, all of them hunted or sought game.""**"
"6010","Abu Bakrah (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade khadhf, throwing pebbles with the fingers. A cousin of his took a pebble and asked about this prohibition, then threw it. Abu Bakrah said he had informed him of the prohibition yet he threw, and he swore by Allah that he would never speak to him in Arabic as long as he lived, and in one narration with a firm oath that he would never speak to him."
"6011","Imran ibn Husayn or Abdullah ibn Mughaffal (رضي الله عنهما) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning khadhf. > **""Beware of throwing pebbles, for it breaks the tooth and blinds the eye, and it does not injure the enemy.""**"
"6012","Al-Husayn ibn Ali (رضي الله عنهما) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""Do not approach birds in their nests by night, for the night is a security for them.""**"
"6013","Amr ibn Yazid reported from his father that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say. > **""There is none who kills a sparrow except that it will cry out on the Day of Resurrection, saying: O Lord, this one killed me wantonly; he neither benefited through killing me, nor did he leave me to live upon Your earth.""**"
"6014","Muadh ibn Jabal (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""Whoever eats or drinks or shoots game and forgets to mention the Name of Allah, let him eat from it, so long as he did not abandon the basmalah deliberately.""**"
"6015","Anas ibn Malik (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, meaning over the slaughtered animal. > **""When you pronounce the Name, magnify as well.""**"
"6016","Abu Hurayrah (رضي الله عنه) reported that a man asked the Prophet ﷺ: What is your view of a man who slaughters and forgets to pronounce the Name? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""The Name of Allah is upon the mouth of every Muslim.""**"
"6017","Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani and Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman (رضي الله عنهما) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""Eat whatever your bow returns to you.""**"
"6018","Ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) reported that a black slave came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked: A wayfarer passes by me while I am among the livestock of my master — may I give him to drink from their milk without their permission? He said no. The man then asked about shooting game that remains before him or disappears from sight. He said. > **""Eat what remains before you, and leave what disappears from you.""**"
"6019","Ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) disliked that game which spent the night away from its hunter should be eaten."
"6020","Ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""When you release your dog and it eats from the game, do not eat, for it held it for itself. And when you release it and it kills without eating, then eat, for it held it for its master.""**"
"6021","Ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) reported that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I release my dog and it catches game. He said. > **""If it eats, do not eat. And if it does not eat, then eat.""**"
"6022","Abu Hurayrah (رضي الله عنه) reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he forbade ramiyyah, that an animal be shot and then eaten, but rather it is to be slaughtered, then they may shoot if they wish. > **""An animal is not to be shot and then eaten; rather it is to be slaughtered, then they may shoot if they wish.""**"
"6023","Samurah (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""Do not take anything possessing a soul as a target.""**"
"6024","Samurah ibn Jundub (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a beast be tied up as a target, and that its meat be eaten when it has been so tied. > **""An animal is not to be tied up as a target, nor is its meat to be eaten when it has been tied up.""**"
"6025","Al-Mughirah ibn Shubah (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Prophet ﷺ passed by a group of the Ansar shooting at a pigeon, and he said. > **""Do not take a living soul as a target.""**"
"6026","Abu Salih al-Hanafi reported from a Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, whom he thought to be Ibn Umar (رضي الله عنهما), that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say. > **""Whoever mutilates one possessing a soul and then does not repent, Allah will mutilate him on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"6027","Abu al-Ahwas reported that his father Awf ibn Malik came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing tattered garments, and he said. > **""O Awf, are your camels not born with sound ears, then you deliberately cut some of them and say: This is a bahirah, and you deliberately slit some of them and say: This is a surm? Do not do so. The forearm of Allah is stronger than your forearm, and the blade of Allah is sharper than your blade. Eat what Allah has given you as lawful, and do not forbid anything of your wealth. O Awf ibn Malik, is the slave who obeys you and follows your command more beloved to you, or the slave who does not obey you nor follow your command more beloved to you? He said: Rather my slave who obeys me and follows my command. He said: So likewise are you before your Lord.""**"
"6028","Abu Said al-Khudri (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Prophet ﷺ was asked about cutting off the fat tails of sheep and the humps of camels, and he said. > **""Whatever is cut from a beast while it is alive is dead meat.""**"
"6029","Qurrah ibn Iyas (رضي الله عنه) reported that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughter a sheep yet I feel mercy for it. The Prophet ﷺ said. > **""If you show mercy to the sheep, Allah will show mercy to you.""**"
"6030","Abu Umamah (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""Whoever shows mercy to a slaughtered animal, Allah will show mercy to him on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"6031","In another narration from Abu Umamah (رضي الله عنه), the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""Whoever shows mercy, even to a sparrow slaughtered, Allah will show mercy to him on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"6032","Maqil ibn Yasar (رضي الله عنه) reported: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I seize a camel to slaughter it, then I feel mercy for it. He said. > **""If you show mercy to it, Allah will show mercy to you.""**"
"6033","Ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man placing his foot upon the side of a sheep while sharpening his blade, as the sheep gazed at him with its eyes. He said. > **""Why not before this? Does he wish to kill it twice over?""**"
"6034","Safinah (رضي الله عنه) reported that a man slaughtered his she-camel with a jidhl, a tree root, then asked the Prophet ﷺ, who commanded them to eat it. > **""Eat it.""**"
"6035","Safinah (رضي الله عنه) reported in the narration of al-Bazzar that he shed the blood of a camel with a jidhl, then asked the Prophet ﷺ about it. He asked whether it caused the blood to flow. He said yes, so he commanded him to eat it. > **""Did it cause the blood to flow? Then eat it.""**"
"6036","Ibn Umar (رضي الله عنهما) reported that a woman pasturing sheep for the family of Kab ibn Malik at Sal feared one sheep would die, so she slaughtered it with a stone. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he commanded them to eat it. In another narration, Kab ibn Malik asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a slave-girl who slaughtered with a sharp stone, and he said. > **""Eat it.""**"
"6037","Abu Rafi (رضي الله عنه) reported: I slaughtered a sheep with a peg, then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered a sheep with a peg? He said. > **""Eat it.""**"
"6038","Hudhayfah (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""Slaughter with everything that severs the jugular veins, except tooth and nail.""**"
"6039","Abu Umamah (رضي الله عنه) reported that a slave-girl of Abu Masud Uqbah ibn Amr was pasturing sheep when one was dying, so she broke a stone from al-Marwah and slaughtered it with it. She brought it to Uqbah ibn Amr and informed him, so he said: Take it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as you are. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked her whether she had severed the jugular veins. She said yes. He said. > **""Everything that severs the jugular veins is permissible, so long as it is not the edge of a tooth or the edge of a nail.""**"
"6040","Zirr ibn Hubaysh reported: The people of Madinah went out in a military expedition, when a tall bald man wearing a coarse waist-wrapper and a striped cloak stood above the people by a forearm and said: O people, emigrate and do not speak ill; let none of you strike a hare with a stick or a stone and then eat it; rather slaughter with the asal, spears and arrows. I asked who he was, and they said: Umar ibn al-Khattab (رضي الله عنه)."
"6041","Anas (رضي الله عنه) reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he was asked: Is slaughter only in the throat and the labbah? He said. > **""Had you stabbed it in its thigh, it would have sufficed you.""**"
"6042","Rafi ibn Khadij (رضي الله عنه) reported from the Prophet ﷺ that a camel of the charity camels fled, and they pursued it. When they were unable to seize it, a man shot it with an arrow and struck its fatal spot. They asked about eating it, so he commanded them to eat it, and said. > **""They have wild instincts like the wildness of wild beasts. When any of them eludes you, do with it as you did with this one, then eat it.""**"
"6043","Rafi (رضي الله عنه) reported: We were with the Prophet ﷺ at Dhu al-Hulayfah in Tihamah. A riding camel fell into a well in Madinah and was slaughtered from its flank, meaning its side, and Umar (رضي الله عنه) took a tenth of it for a dirham."
"6044","Jabir ibn Abdullah (رضي الله عنهما) reported: We pursued a cow in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to restrain it, but it escaped us and resisted us. A freedman of ours called Dhakwan confronted it with a sword in his hand while it roamed about, until it headed toward a mound. When it passed him he struck it with the sword at the root of its neck or upon its shoulder, tearing it open, and it fell before its proper slaughter could be attained. I and Abdullah ibn Thabit ibn al-Jidh went out and met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned its case to him, and he said. > **""Eat. When any of these beasts eludes you, restrain it as you restrain wild game.""**"
"6045","Ali (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""All grazing beasts are unruly.""**"
"6046","Abu al-Darda and Abu Umamah (رضي الله عنهما) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother.""**"
"6047","Jabir (رضي الله عنه) reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said. > **""The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother, when it has grown hair.""**"
"6048","Ibn Umar (رضي الله عنهما) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother, when it has grown hair.""**"
"6049","Kab ibn Malik (رضي الله عنه) reported from the Prophet ﷺ concerning the slaughter of the fetus. > **""Its slaughter is the slaughter of its mother.""**"
"6050","Abu Ayyub (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Prophet ﷺ said. > **""The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother.""**"
"6051","Abu Layla (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the slaughter of the fetus, and he said. > **""Its slaughter is the slaughter of its mother.""**"
"6052","Ibn Umar (رضي الله عنهما) raised it to the Prophet ﷺ, saying he said. > **""Every creature of land and sea that has no blood which flows has no slaughter required for it.""**"
"6053","Abu Said al-Khudri (رضي الله عنه) reported: Some Bedouins used to bring us meat, and we felt unease about it in ourselves, so we mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said. > **""Bind them by firm oaths that they slaughtered it, then mention the Name of Allah and eat.""**"
"6054","Ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) said: The slaughtered animals of the Jews and Christians were made lawful because they believed in the Torah and the Gospel."
"6055","Al-Irbad ibn Sariyah (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the slaughtered animals of the Christians, and their churches, and their feasts, and he said. > **""If you do not eat it, then feed me.""**"
"6056","Umar (رضي الله عنه) was asked about eating the hare, so he called for Ammar. When Ammar came, Umar said: Narrate to us the hadith of the hare from when we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in such-and-such place. Ammar said: A Bedouin presented a hare to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who commanded the people to eat. The Bedouin said he had seen blood. He said it is nothing, then said come near and eat. The man said he was fasting. He asked fasting what? He said fasting three days of every month. He said: Why did you not make them the white days? > **""It is nothing. Come near and eat. Why did you not make them the white days?""**"
"6057","Ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) reported: A hare was presented to the Prophet ﷺ while Aishah (رضي الله عنها) was asleep, so he set aside a thigh for her from it. When she awoke he gave it to her, and she ate it."
"6058","Abdurrahman ibn Hasanah (رضي الله عنه) reported: We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey. We halted in a land abounding with lizards. We caught some and slaughtered them. While the pots boiled with them, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said. > **""A nation of the Children of Israel was lost, and I fear lest these be they, so overturn them.""**"
"6059","Abdurrahman ibn Ghanm (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""A tribe of the Children of Israel perished, and it is not known where they perished, and I fear lest these lizards be they.""**"
"6060","Samurah ibn Jundub (رضي الله عنه) reported: A Bedouin man of Banu Fazarah came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ while he was delivering the sermon, interrupted his sermon, and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say concerning the lizard? He said. > **""A nation of the Children of Israel was transformed, and I do not know which beasts they were transformed into.""**"
"6061","Aishah (رضي الله عنها) reported that a lizard was presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but he did not eat it. Aishah said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not feed it to the poor? He said. > **""Do not feed them from what you do not eat.""**"
"6062","Hudhayfah (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""The lizard is a nation that was transformed into vermin of the earth.""**"
"6063","Samurah (رضي الله عنه) reported that a man asked the Prophet ﷺ: What is your view concerning the lizard? He said it was a transformed nation, and Allah knows best. Uyaynah ibn Badr entered and saw a cupper cupping the Prophet ﷺ with a horn, and said: Do you allow this man over your flesh? He said. > **""It is a transformed nation, and Allah knows best. This cupping is the best of what you treat yourselves with.""**"
"6064","Samurah (رضي الله عنه) reported that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking a ruling about the lizard, and he said. > **""I neither command it nor forbid anyone from it, except that we, the family of Muhammad, do not eat it.""**"
"6065","Ibn Umar (رضي الله عنهما) was asked about the lizard, and he said: Since the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning it what he said, we have refrained from eating it."
"6066","Abu Maryam (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Prophet ﷺ forbade eating the lizard. > **""Eating the lizard is forbidden.""**"
"6067","Ibn Umar (رضي الله عنهما) reported: A lizard was eaten in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he found it distasteful, and we find distasteful what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ found distasteful."
"6068","Maymunah, wife of the Prophet ﷺ (رضي الله عنها), reported: My sister Umm Hufaydah presented lizards to me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from Isha with Khalid, her nephew, and I presented the lizards to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached out, thinking they were chickens. I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you know what this is? He said no, then withheld his hand. I said: These are lizards. He said it is the food of the Bedouins. Khalid said: Is it unlawful? He said no. So Khalid ate from it before him while he ﷺ looked on. > **""That is the food of the Bedouins. No.""**"
"6069","Maymunah (رضي الله عنها) reported that a lizard was presented to her, and two men of her people came to her. She had it prepared and set it before them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came while they were eating and welcomed them, then took to eat. When he raised a morsel to his mouth he asked what this was. She said: A lizard presented to us. She said: He put down the morsel, and the two men wished to cast out what was in their mouths, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""Do not do so. You, the people of Najd, eat it, while we, the people of Tihamah, dislike it.""**"
"6070","Al-Shabi reported: I sat with Ibn Umar for two years, or a year and a half, and never heard him narrate anything from the Prophet ﷺ, except that once he narrated from a wife of the Prophet ﷺ that the Prophet ﷺ was brought a lizard, and the Prophet ﷺ said. > **""Eat it, there is no harm in it, but it is not the food of my people.""**"
"6071","Abu Hurayrah (رضي الله عنه) reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought seven lizards with dates and ghee upon them, and he said. > **""Eat, for I abstain from it.""**"
"6072","Abu Ishaq reported: I was sitting with Abdurrahman ibn Abdullah when a man came asking about his son al-Qasim, saying he went in the morning to al-Kunasah seeking lizards. He asked: Do you eat it? Abdurrahman said: And who forbade it? I heard Abdullah ibn Masud (رضي الله عنه) say: One who forbids the lawful is like one who permits the unlawful."
"6073","Abu Zuhayr al-Numayri (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. > **""Do not kill locusts, for they are the greatest army of Allah.""**"
"6074","Jabir ibn Abdullah (رضي الله عنهما) reported: We raided with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found locusts, and we ate them."
"6075","Abu Umamah (رضي الله عنه) reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Maryam (peace be upon her) asked her Lord for meat without blood in it, so He fed her locusts. She said. > **""O Allah, give it life without suckling, and continue it without satiety.""**"
"6076","Ali ibn Abdullah al-Bariqi reported: A woman in Makkah sought my ruling, so I said: Here is Abdullah ibn Umar, go to him and ask him. She hastened toward him, and I followed her to hear what she said. She said: O Abdullah, give me a ruling about locusts? He said: All of it is lawful slaughtered."
"6077","Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Sadi reported: Some people of my tribe commanded me to ask Said ibn al-Musayyab about sharpened stakes they fix in the earth which by morning have killed a hyena — does he consider that its slaughter? I sat with Said ibn al-Musayyab, and with him was an aged white-haired and white-bearded man of the people of Sham. I asked him about that, and he said: Do you indeed eat the hyena? I said: I never ate it, though some of my people eat it. He said: Eating it is not lawful. The old man said: O servant of Allah, shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from Abu al-Darda, narrating from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? I said: Yes. He said: I heard Abu al-Darda say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade every plunderer, and every mutilated target, and every fanged beast of prey. Said said: He spoke the truth. In one narration, every snatcher instead of every plunderer. > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade every plunderer, and every mutilated target, and every fanged beast of prey.""**"
"6078","Abu Umamah (رضي الله عنه) reported: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a campaign he undertook, and he commanded a crier who announced. In one narration, every predatory beast with claws or fangs. > **""Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient one. Verily domestic donkeys are unlawful, and every possessor of fangs — or he said: of claws. And every predatory beast with claws or fangs.""**"
"6079","Abdurrahman ibn Sahl, who was one of the nuqaba, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the meat of the lizard, and domestic donkeys, and every fanged beast of prey. > **""The meat of the lizard, and domestic donkeys, and every fanged beast of prey are forbidden.""**"
"6080","Abdurrahman ibn Mughaffal al-Sulami reported that he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: I said: What do you say concerning the hyena? He said I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it. I said: What is not forbidden, I eat from it. I said: What do you say concerning the hare? He said I do not eat it, nor do I declare it unlawful. I said: What you do not declare unlawful, I eat. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say concerning the fox? He said does anyone eat that? I said: What do you say concerning the wolf? He said does anyone eat that? > **""I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it. I do not eat it, nor do I declare it unlawful. Does anyone eat that? Does anyone eat that?""**"
"6081","Wabisah ibn Mabad (رضي الله عنه) reported: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, and I heard the Prophet ﷺ say concerning the fox, meaning the fox. > **""Do not take the backs of beasts as pulpits. The worst of beasts is the fox.""**"
"6082","Aishah (رضي الله عنها) said: I marvel at one who eats the crow, though the Prophet ﷺ permitted its killing and named it a transgressor? By Allah, it is not of the wholesome things."
"6083","Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr (رضي الله عنهما) said: Who eats the crow, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named it a transgressor?"
"6084","Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, visited him, so he turned to a goat to slaughter it and it bleated, and he heard its bleating. > **""O Jabir, do not cut off milk, nor progeny.""**"
"6085","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, halted at a lodging and went for his need, then returned while a man had set fire upon a colony of ants, either in the earth or upon a tree, so he asked who had done this, and the man acknowledged it. > **""Extinguish it, extinguish it.""**"
"6086","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that they were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he passed by a colony of ants that had been burned. > **""It is not fitting for a human to punish with the punishment of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.""**"
"6087","Sahl ibn Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing the ant, the bee, the hoopoe, the shrike, and the frog. > **""The Prophet forbade killing the ant, the bee, the hoopoe, the shrike, and the frog.""**"
"6088","Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning flies and the prohibition of killing bees and of burning food in enemy land. > **""All flies are in the Fire except the bee.""**"
"6089","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke of the lifespan of the fly and its end, excepting the bee. > **""The lifespan of the fly is forty nights, and all flies are in the Fire except the bee.""**"
"6090","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning flies. > **""All flies are in the Fire except the bee.""**"
"6091","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing the frog and explained its croaking. > **""Its croaking is glorification.""**"
"6092","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing every living soul, except one that causes harm. > **""The Messenger forbade killing every living soul, except one that causes harm.""**"
"6093","Al-Hasan reported that he witnessed Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, ordering in his sermon the killing of dogs and the slaughter of pigeons kept for gambling and distraction."
"6094","Abu Rafi, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded him to kill every dog. He then found some Ansari women at al-Surayn near al-Baqi who kept a dog, and they complained that their men had been honoured by the Prophet with expeditions while the dog hindered visitors, so that none could approach until a woman stood between him and it, and they asked him to mention it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, which he did. > **""O Abu Rafi, kill it, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will protect them.""**"
"6095","Abu Rafi, may Allah be pleased with him, reported in another narration that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded him to kill dogs, so he went out killing every dog he saw until he aimed at a dog circling a house, whereupon a person from inside called out asking what he intended. He said he intended to kill it, and she said she was a neglected woman whose dog drove beasts from her and alerted her to visitors, so he returned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with her case. > **""O Abu Rafi, kill every dog.""**"
"6096","Abu Rafi, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that Jibril, peace be upon him, sought permission to enter upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and was permitted, but delayed. So the Messenger took his cloak and rose to him while he stood at the door, saying permission had been given, to which he replied that they do not enter a house containing a dog or an image. Then a puppy was found in one of their houses. Abu Rafi said he was commanded in the morning and left no dog but killed it, except that he pitied a distant woman whose dog barked to guard her and left it, then returned under command and killed it. The people asked what was lawful for them of this species ordered to be killed, so Allah revealed the verse concerning lawful good things. > **""Indeed, we do not enter a house in which there is a dog, nor an image.""**"
"6097","Ubaydullah ibn Ali reported from his grandmother Salma, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Abu Rafi, may Allah be pleased with him, to Banu Umayyah ibn Yazid to kill dogs, and sent another man elsewhere with the same order. > **""The Messenger sent Abu Rafi to Banu Umayyah ibn Yazid to kill dogs, and sent another man to kill dogs.""**"
"6098","Jabir al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered the dogs of Madinah to be killed. Then Ibn Umm Maktum, may Allah be pleased with him, came and said his dwelling was distant and he kept a dog, so he was licensed for some days, then killing of his dog was ordered. > **""The Messenger ordered the dogs of Madinah to be killed.""**"
"6099","Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered the killing of large-eyed dogs. > **""The Messenger ordered the killing of the dogs of al-Ayn.""**"
"6100","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that were dogs not a nation among nations he would have ordered every jet-black dog killed, and that the prominent-eyed among them should be killed, for it is accursed from the jinn. > **""Were dogs not a nation among nations, I would have ordered every jet-black dog killed, so kill the prominent-eyed among dogs, for it is accursed from the jinn.""**"
"6101","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to kill dogs. The people of Madinah said they benefited from them among sheep and crops. > **""Kill dogs, then kill from them the jet-black.""**"
"6102","Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said were dogs not a nation among nations he would have ordered them killed, and commanded killing every jet-black dog. > **""Were dogs not a nation among nations, I would have ordered them killed, so kill from them every jet-black dog.""**"
"6103","Usamah, meaning Ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that he entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while gloom was upon him, and asked his state. He said Jibril, peace be upon him, had promised to come yet had not come for three days. A dog was there, so Usamah placed his hand upon his head and cried out. When asked, he said it was a dog, so the Prophet ordered it and it was killed. Then Jibril came to him, and he asked why he had not come though he never broke his promise to him. > **""We do not enter a house in which there is a dog, nor images.""**"
"6104","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog."
"6105","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say that the angels do not enter a house containing a dog. > **""The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog.""**"
"6106","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke of one who keeps a dog that is neither for hunting nor for livestock. > **""Whoever keeps a dog that is neither a hunting dog nor for livestock, a qirat decreases from his reward every day.""**"
"6107","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke of one who keeps a dog that is neither for hunting nor for livestock. > **""Whoever keeps a dog that is neither a hunting dog nor for livestock, a qirat decreases from his reward every day.""**"
"6108","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke of one who keeps a dog that is neither for livestock nor for hunting. > **""Whoever keeps a dog that is neither for livestock nor a hunting dog, two qirats decrease from his reward every day.""**"
"6109","Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, described the jet-black dog. > **""The jet-black dog is a devil.""**"
"6110","Usamah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that he entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while gloom was upon him, and asked his state. He said Jibril had not come to him for three days. Then a puppy was found between his houses, so he ordered it and it was killed. Then Jibril, peace be upon him, appeared to him, so the Messenger hastened toward him when he saw him and asked why he had not come. > **""We do not enter a house in which there is a dog, nor images.""**"
"6111","Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that Jibril was withheld from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he asked what had withheld him. > **""We do not enter a house in which there is a dog.""**"
"6112","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to visit the quarter of some Ansar while another quarter lay before them, and it distressed them, so they said he visited the others and not them. He explained it was because of a dog in their quarter. When they noted the others kept a cat, he explained its nature. > **""Because in your quarter there is a dog. The cat is a predator.""**"
"6113","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, described the cat. > **""The cat is a predator.""**"
"6114","Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke of killing the snake and the gecko, and of abandoning the snake from fear of its consequence. > **""Whoever kills a snake, for him are seven good deeds, and whoever kills a gecko, for him is one good deed, and whoever leaves a snake fearing its consequence is not from us.""**"
"6115","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned the snake and said it and man were created alike, so that when it sees him it frightens him, and when it bites him it pains him. > **""It was created equal with man; if it sees him it frightens him, and if it bites him it pains him, so kill them wherever you find them.""**"
"6116","Sarra bint Nabhan al-Ghanawiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that her slave Nusayb asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about snakes, which of them should be killed, and she heard him answer to kill what appears of them, large and small, black and white, and that killing them would be ransom from the Fire while being killed by them was martyrdom. > **""Kill what appears of them, their large and their small, their black and their white, for whoever of my Ummah kills one, it will be his ransom from the Fire, and whoever is killed by one will be a martyr.""**"
"6117","Abu al-Ahwas al-Jushami reported that while Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, was preaching, a snake appeared walking upon the wall, so he broke his sermon and struck it with his staff until he killed it, then said he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, speak of killing snakes and scorpions. > **""Whoever kills a snake, it is as if he killed a polytheist whose blood had become lawful.""**"
"6118","Uthman ibn Abi al-As, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned snakes and said whoever feared their retaliation was not from us. > **""Whoever fears their retaliation is not from us.""**"
"6119","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded killing snakes and warned against fearing their retaliation. > **""Kill snakes, and whoever fears their retaliation is not from me.""**"
"6120","Dawud ibn Abd al-Jabbar reported that he was with Ibrahim ibn Jarir at a funeral while he rode, and when they reached the graveyard a snake emerged. Ibrahim said his father told him he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say whoever saw a snake and left it from fear of it had no bond with him. > **""Whoever sees a snake and does not kill it from fear of it is not from me.""**"
"6121","Jarir, may Allah be pleased with him, also reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanding the killing of all snakes and warning whoever left them fearing retaliation. > **""Kill all snakes; whoever leaves one fearing its retaliation is not from me.""**"
"6122","Abu Layla, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever saw a snake and left it from fear of seeking revenge was not from us. > **""Whoever sees a snake and does not kill it fearing its pursuit is not from us.""**"
"6123","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded killing snakes, especially the one with two stripes and the short-tailed, for they snatch sight and abort the fetus, and whoever did not kill them was not from us. > **""Kill snakes, and kill Dhu al-Tufyatayn and the Abtar, for they snatch sight and abort the fetus, and whoever does not kill them is not from us.""**"
"6124","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that snakes are the transformed ones of the jinn, as monkeys and pigs were transformed from the Children of Israel. > **""Snakes are the transformed ones of the jinn, as monkeys and pigs were transformed from the Children of Israel.""**"
"6125","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said they had never made peace with snakes since warring them, so whoever saw any should kill it, for their Muslims would not appear, and whoever left any from fear was not from us. > **""We have never made peace with snakes since we warred them, so whoever sees any of them, let him kill it, for their Muslims will not appear to you, and whoever leaves any of them from fear is not from us.""**"
"6126","Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded killing all snakes except the short-tailed house snake and the one with two stripes upon its back, for they kill the child in its mother's belly and obscure sight, and whoever left them was not from us. > **""Kill all snakes except the short-tailed house snake and Dhu al-Tufyatayn upon its back, for they kill the child in its mother's belly and obscure sight, and whoever leaves them is not from us.""**"
"6127","Uthman, meaning Ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said a single strike of the whip sufficed against the snake, whether it hit or missed. > **""One strike of the whip suffices you against the snake, whether you hit it or miss it.""**"
"6128","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded killing the gecko even in the hollow of the Kaaba. > **""Kill the gecko, even in the hollow of the Kaaba.""**"
"6129","Uqbah ibn Fakih reported that he went to Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, who came out holding a spear. When asked about the spear at that hour, he said he sought the wicked beast for killing which Allah writes a good deed and erases an evil deed, namely the gecko."
"6130","Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that she heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say that Allah erases seven sins from one who kills a gecko. > **""Whoever kills a gecko, Allah erases seven sins from him.""**"
"6131","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, used to order snakes killed until Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir, may Allah be pleased with him, told him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing snakes found in houses. He also reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went to touch the Black Stone when a scorpion stung him, and he reproached it, saying had it spared any it would have spared the Prophet. > **""The Prophet forbade killing the snakes found in houses. What is with you? May Allah curse you! Had you spared any, you would have spared the Prophet.""**"
"6132","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing the residents of houses except Dhu al-Tufyatayn and the Abtar, for they blind and cause women to miscarry. > **""The Messenger forbade killing the residents of houses, except Dhu al-Tufyatayn and the Abtar, for they blind and cause women to miscarry.""**"
"6133","Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing house snakes except the Abtar and Dhu al-Tufyatayn, for they snatch or blot sight and abort the fetus, and whoever left them was not from us. > **""The Messenger forbade killing house snakes, except the Abtar and Dhu al-Tufyatayn, for they snatch sight and abort the fetus, and whoever leaves them is not from us.""**"
"6134","Sahl ibn Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that a newlywed Ansari youth went out with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on an expedition, then returned along the way to look at his family. He found his wife standing in the room and levelled his spear at her, but she told him to enter and see what was in the house. He entered and found a snake coiled upon his bed, so he pierced it with his spear and planted the spear in the courtyard. The snake convulsed and the man convulsed, and both died. When it was mentioned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he explained the presence of Muslim jinn in Madinah and residents in these houses, commanding seeking refuge upon seeing them and killing them if they returned. > **""Muslim jinn have settled in Madinah, and these houses have residents; when you see any of them, seek refuge from it, and if it returns, kill it.""**"
"6135","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that a newlywed man was sent with an expedition dispatched by the Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. When he returned he hastened to his family and found his wife standing at her door, so jealousy seized him and he readied his spear to stab her. She told him not to hasten but to see what was in the house. He entered and found a snake coiled upon her bed, so he stabbed it and it died, and the man also died. When it reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he explained that these houses have residents from the jinn and forbade killing them without warning. > **""These houses have residents from the jinn.""**"
"6136","Abdullah ibn Jafar, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that killing them was forbidden, meaning the snakes found in houses. > **""Killing them was forbidden, meaning the snakes found in houses.""**"
"6137","Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that when Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, proposed to Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said a bride must have a walimah. Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, said a ram was upon him, and another said such-and-such grain was upon him. > **""A bride must have a walimah.""**"
"6138","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said feeding on the day of the wedding was Sunnah, feeding two days bounty, and feeding three days show and repute. > **""Food of one day at the wedding is Sunnah, food of two days is bounty, and food of three days is show and repute.""**"
"6139","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, said the walimah of the first day is a right, of the second bounty, and of the third show and repute, and whoever seeks repute, Allah will expose him thereby."
"6140","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married Safiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, and made her freedom her dowry, and held the walimah for three days. He spread a leather mat brought by Umm Sulaym, may Allah be pleased with her, cast upon it dried yogurt and dates, and fed the people for three days. > **""The Messenger married Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry, and held the walimah for three days.""**"
"6141","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not hold a walimah for any of his wives except Safiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her. > **""The Messenger did not hold a walimah for any of his wives except Safiyyah.""**"
"6142","Sahl ibn Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, held a walimah for Safiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her. When asked what was in it, he said there was nothing but dates and sawiq. > **""There was nothing in his walimah but dates and sawiq.""**"
"6143","Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that when Safiyyah bint Huyay, may Allah be pleased with her, was brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in his tent, people attended, and he attended among them for a share. The Prophet came out with about a mudd and a half of Ajwah dates in his cloak and told them to eat. > **""Eat from your mother's walimah.""**"
"6144","Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, held a walimah for one of his wives with two mudds of barley. > **""The Prophet held a walimah for one of his wives with two mudds of barley.""**"
"6145","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, held a walimah for one of his wives with a pot of harisah. > **""The Prophet held a walimah for one of his wives with a pot of harisah.""**"
"6146","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, held a walimah for Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, with dates and ghee. > **""The Messenger held a walimah for Umm Salamah with dates and ghee.""**"
"6147","Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that they attended the wedding of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and never saw a wedding better in beauty. The Messenger prepared raisins and dates for them, so they ate, and her bedding on the wedding night was a ram's skin. > **""We attended the wedding of Ali and Fatimah, and never saw a wedding more beautiful; he prepared raisins and dates for us, and her bedding was a ram's skin.""**"
"6148","Sahl ibn Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that Abu Usayd, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married a woman and invited the Prophet to his wedding. His wife, though the bride, served them date infusion steeped overnight and strained. > **""Abu Usayd married and invited the Prophet to his wedding, and his bride served date nabidh steeped overnight and strained.""**"
"6149","Asma, meaning bint Umays, may Allah be pleased with her, said she presented your grandmother Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, to your grandfather Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and the stuffing of her bed and pillow was nothing but fiber. Ali held a walimah for Fatimah, and no walimah in that time was better than his, for he mortgaged his armor with a Jew for half a measure of barley. > **""Her bedding and pillow were stuffed with nothing but fiber, and Ali mortgaged his armor with a Jew for barley for the walimah.""**"
"6150","Shahr ibn Hawshab reported that Asma bint Yazid ibn al-Sakan, may Allah be pleased with her, one of the women of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, served him food and he said he did not desire it. She told him she had adorned Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then called him to her unveiling. He came and sat beside her, was brought a cup of milk and drank, then handed it to her, but she lowered her head in shyness. Asma scolded her to take from the Messenger's hand, so she took and drank something. He then told her to give her companion, but Asma asked the Prophet to drink again and hand it to her from his hand. He drank and handed it to her, so she sat with it upon her knees, turning it to follow the Prophet's drinking place. He then told her to hand it to the women with her, but they said they did not desire it, so he warned them against combining hunger and falsehood. Asma then asked the narrator whether he would refrain from saying he did not desire it, and he vowed never to return to it. > **""Give it to them. Do not combine hunger and falsehood.""**"
"6151","Asma bint Umays, may Allah be pleased with her, said she was the companion of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who prepared her and brought her to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with other women. They found no hospitality with him but a cup of milk, from which he drank then handed it to Aisha. The girl felt shy, so they told her not to refuse the Messenger's hand and to take from it, so she took shyly and drank. He then told her to hand it to her companions, but they said they did not desire it, so he warned them. When asked whether saying she did not desire what she desired counted as falsehood, he explained that falsehood is written as falsehood until even a small lie is written as a small lie. > **""Hand it to your companions. Do not combine hunger and falsehood. Falsehood is written as falsehood, until even a small lie is written as a small lie.""**"
"6152","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to hold a walimah even with a sheep. > **""O Abu Hurayrah, hold a walimah even with a sheep.""**"
"6153","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, dyed with yellow. He asked about the dye and whether he had married, and he said yes. When asked whether he had held a walimah, he said no, so the Messenger tossed to him a gold nugget and told him to hold one. > **""What is this dye? Have you married? Have you held a walimah? Hold a walimah even with a sheep.""**"
"6154","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wearing a yellow garment. He said Mahyam, a word used when asking about a matter, and he said he had married. When asked for how much, he said for the weight of a gold nugget, so he commanded a walimah. Anas said they valued it as a quarter dinar. > **""Mahyam? For how much? Hold a walimah even with a sheep.""**"
"6155","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded answering the inviter, not refusing gifts, and not striking Muslims. In one narration, answer the inviter when invited. > **""Answer the inviter, do not refuse gifts, and do not strike Muslims.""**"
"6156","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said the walimah is a right and a Sunnah, so whoever is invited and does not answer has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger, while concerning khars, idhar, and tawkir one has a choice. Khars is for birth, idhar for circumcision, and tawkir when a man builds a house and settles among people, prepares food and invites them, so they may come or stay as they wish."
"6157","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever invited them should be answered. > **""Whoever invites you, answer him.""**"
"6158","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said when one of them was invited to food he should answer; if not fasting he should eat, and if fasting he should supplicate for blessing. > **""When one of you is invited to food, let him answer; if he is not fasting, let him eat, and if he is fasting, let him supplicate for blessing.""**"
"6159","Ya'la ibn Murrah (رضي الله عنه) was invited to a feast and sat while fasting, while the people ate and he did not taste. They said had they known he was fasting they would not have invited him, so he told them not to say that, and reported what he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning answering a brother. > **""Answer your brother, for you are in one of two positions with him: either good, and you most deserve to have witnessed it, or otherwise, and you forbid him from it and enjoin good upon him.""**"
"6160","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (رضي الله عنه) prepared food for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions, and the Prophet ﷺ addressed a man who excused himself by fasting. > **""Your brother invited you and went to trouble for you, yet you say: I am fasting? Break your fast and fast a day in its place if you wish.""**"
"6161","Qays ibn Abi Hazim (رحمه الله) stated the conduct of one who is fasting when food or drink is offered to him."
"6162","Abdullah ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) reported that even a man from al-'Awali inviting the Prophet ﷺ at midnight to barley bread would find him accepting."
"6163","Abdullah ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning his readiness to accept invitation. > **""If I were invited to a shank, I would surely accept.""**"
"6164","Ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) reported from the Prophet ﷺ concerning the food of the walimah to which only the satiated are called. > **""The worst food is the food of the walimah to which the rich is invited and the poor is left. Wretched is the food of the walimah to which the satiated is invited and from which the hungry is withheld.""**"
"6165","Ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning boasting of forefathers who died in Jahiliyyah, with a parable of a king, his servants, and an angel. > **""Do not boast of your forefathers who died in Jahiliyyah. Shall I not inform you? The example of your forefathers who died in Jahiliyyah is like a king who built a palace by the roadside and placed food therein and appointed men over it, saying: None shall pass but shall partake of this food of mine. When a man passed in fine appearance and fine clothes they went to him, clung to him, and brought him to eat of that food. And when a man came in poor appearance and worn clothes they barred him. When that prolonged, Allah sent an angel from the angels in poor appearance and worn clothes, so he passed by them, and they rose against him and thrust him away. He said to them: I am hungry, and food is but made for the hungry. They said: The king's food is eaten only by the righteous. So they thrust him away and he departed. Then he came in a handsome form and fine clothes, passing as though not intending them, at a distance from them. So they went to him, clung to him, and said: Come, partake of the king's food. He said: I do not want it. They said: The king will not leave you if it reaches him that one like you passed and did not partake of food; it will grieve him, and we fear punishment from him will befall us. So they compelled him and brought him to the food and set the food before him, whereupon he did thus with his clothes. They said: What are you doing? He said: I came to you in poor appearance and worn clothes and told you I was hungry, yet you barred me. And I came to you in fine appearance and fine clothes, so you compelled me and overcame me and refused but to invite me. So may you be disgraced, and may your king be disgraced; your king makes this food only for the world, and he has no portion with Allah. Then the angel ascended, and punishment descended upon them.""**"
"6166","Imran ibn Husayn (رضي الله عنه) reported the Prophet's ﷺ prohibition concerning the food of the defiantly disobedient. > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade answering the invitation to the food of the fasiqin.""**"
"6167","Abdullah ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) stated what is of the Sunnah for a host when his brother departs."
"6168","Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar (رحمهم الله) reported his wedding in his father's lifetime, when Abu Ayyub al-Ansari (رضي الله عنه) saw the house veiled with green hangings, reproached them for draping walls and for being overcome by women, and refused to eat or enter, then departed."
"6169","Suhayb (رضي الله عنه) reported that he prepared a small meal for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he sat among men, exchanged gestures with him concerning his companions, and at last included them, whereupon all ate to satiety and food remained. > **""And these? And these?""**"
"6170","Samurah ibn Jundub (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid an invited man bringing another unless the hosts permit. > **""When a man is invited to food, he must not bring anyone with him unless the people of the food permit him.""**"
"6171","Abu Shu'ayb al-Ansari (رضي الله عنه) reported that he perceived hunger in the Prophet's ﷺ face, prepared food for five through his butcher slave, and invited the Prophet ﷺ, who came with four others while an extra man followed them, whereupon the Prophet ﷺ spoke at the door. > **""This man followed us; if you wish, give him permission, otherwise he will return.""**"
"6172","Aishah (رضي الله عنها) reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning one who intrudes upon food to which he was not called. > **""Whoever intrudes upon people for food to which he was not invited enters as a transgressor and eats unlawful. Whoever intrudes upon people for food to which he was not invited and eats anything thereof eats unlawful.""**"
"6173","Ibn Umar (رضي الله عنهما) reported in marfu' form from the Prophet ﷺ concerning coming to food without invitation. > **""Whoever comes to food to which he was not invited enters as a thief and eats unlawful.""**"
"6174","Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (رضي الله عنه) said that in Jahiliyyah the imma'ah was the intruder upon food, whereas among his contemporaries it is he who mortgages his religion."
"6175","Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (رضي الله عنه) reported in another wording that the imma'ah was once the follower of an invited man, but today is he who subjects his religion to men, and that what was once called samar of falsehood is today qila wa qala."
"6176","Mu'adh ibn Jabal (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ attended the marriage of a Companion, supplicated for him, ordered beating the duff at his head, and addressed the people when trays of fruit and sugar were brought and they withheld their hands. > **""Upon goodness and blessing and affection, and auspicious fortune, and expansiveness in provision. May Allah bless you. Beat the duff at his head. What is with you that you do not plunder? I only forbade you the plunder of armies; as for weddings, there is no prohibition.""**"
"6177","Abu Mas'ud (رضي الله عنه) is reported to have forbidden snatching and plundering at the wedding feast."
"6178","Ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning feeding on the days of the wedding. > **""Food of one day at the wedding is Sunnah, food of two days is merit, and food of three days is show and seeking repute.""**"
"6179","Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (رضي الله عنه) said that the walimah on the first day is due, on the second is merit, and on the third is show and repute, and Allah will expose him who seeks repute."
"6180","Abu Rafi', freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ (رضي الله عنه), reported that when al-Hasan ibn Ali (رضي الله عنهما) was born, Fatimah (رضي الله عنها) intended 'aqiqah with two rams, whereupon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ directed her otherwise, and she did the like for al-Husayn thereafter. > **""Do not make 'aqiqah for him, but shave his head, then give in charity its weight in silver in the path of Allah.""**"
"6181","Abu Rafi' (رضي الله عنه) reported in another wording that Fatimah (رضي الله عنها) asked about 'aqiqah with blood for al-Hasan (رضي الله عنه), and the Prophet ﷺ directed her to shaving and charity, the Awqas being needy Companions of Suffah. > **""No, but shave his head, then give in charity the weight of his hair in silver upon the poor and the Awqas.""**"
"6182","Anas ibn Malik (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the heads of al-Hasan and al-Husayn (رضي الله عنهما) shaved on their seventh day, silver given equal to the weight, as he found no animal to slaughter."
"6183","A man of Banu Damrah from his father (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about 'aqiqah and expressed dislike of the term 'uquq, then gave permission for sacrifice. > **""I do not love 'uquq. Whoever has a child born to him and wishes to sacrifice on behalf of his child, let him do so.""**"
"6184","The same Damri report is transmitted in another wording through his father or through his uncle."
"6185","Umm Salamah (رضي الله عنها) reported from the Prophet ﷺ concerning 'aqiqah and leaving it to desire. > **""Whoever has a child born to him and wishes to sacrifice on his behalf, let him do so.""**"
"6186","Asma bint Yazid (رضي الله عنها) reported from the Prophet ﷺ concerning the due 'aqiqah for male and female. > **""'Aqiqah is due upon the boy: two equal sheep, and upon the girl: one sheep.""**"
"6187","Jabir ibn Abdullah (رضي الله عنهما) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn (رضي الله عنهما)."
"6188","Anas (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn with two rams."
"6189","Aishah (رضي الله عنها) stated the rule of 'aqiqah and reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two sheep each for al-Hasan and al-Husayn on the seventh day, ordered removal of harm from the head, instructed what to say at slaughter, and replaced the Jahili practice of blood with khaluq perfume. > **""Slaughter upon his name and say: In the name of Allah, Allah is Greatest. O Allah, from You and to You, this is the 'aqiqah of so-and-so.""**"
"6190","Abu Hurayrah (رضي الله عنه) reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the practice of the Jews and the command to differ from them. > **""The Jews make 'aqiqah for the boy with one ram and make no 'aqiqah for the girl. So make 'aqiqah — or slaughter — for the boy with two rams, and for the girl with one ram.""**"
"6191","Abu Hurayrah (رضي الله عنه) reported from the Prophet ﷺ concerning the newborn boy. > **""With the boy is an 'aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him.""**"
"6192","Ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) reported from the Prophet ﷺ concerning the number of sacrifices. > **""For the boy are two 'aqiqahs and for the girl is one 'aqiqah.""**"
"6193","Ibn Umar (رضي الله عنهما) reported from the Prophet ﷺ concerning the seventh day of the child. > **""When it is his seventh day, shed blood on his behalf, remove harm from him, and name him.""**"
"6194","Buraydah (رضي الله عنه) reported from the Prophet ﷺ concerning the newborn. > **""Every newborn is pledged by his 'aqiqah.""**"
"6195","Anas (رضي الله عنه) reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the kinds of animals for 'aqiqah. > **""Whoever has a boy born to him, let him make 'aqiqah for him from camels, cattle, and sheep.""**"
"6196","Yazid ibn Abdullah al-Muzani from his father (رضي الله عنهما) reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning fara' and 'aqiqah. > **""In camels is a fara', and in sheep is a fara', and 'aqiqah is made for the boy, but his head is not to be touched with blood.""**"
"6197","Anas (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made 'aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn (رضي الله عنهما) with two rams."
"6198","Ali (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn (رضي الله عنهما)."
"6199","Buraydah (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn (رضي الله عنهما)."
"6200","Jabir (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn and had them circumcised at seven days."
"6201","Qatadah (رحمه الله) reported that Anas ibn Malik (رضي الله عنه) used to perform 'aqiqah for his sons with a jazur camel."
"6202","Buraydah (رضي الله عنه) reported from the Prophet ﷺ concerning the days of slaughter for 'aqiqah. > **""'Aqiqah is slaughtered on the seventh, or the fourteenth, or the twenty-first.""**"
"6203","Anas (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Prophet ﷺ performed 'aqiqah for himself after he was sent as a Prophet."
"6204","Abdullah ibn Abbas (رضي الله عنهما) said there are seven matters of Sunnah for the boy on the seventh day: naming, circumcision, removal of harm, piercing the ear, 'aqiqah, shaving the head, smearing with the blood of his 'aqiqah, and charity of gold or silver equal to the weight of the hair of his head."
"6205","Ali ibn Abi Talib (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ himself named Hasan, Husayn, and Muhsin, performed 'aqiqah for them, had their heads shaved, gave charity equal to the weight, and commanded concerning them so they were made cheerful and circumcised."
"6206","Al-Husayn (رضي الله عنه) reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning adhan in the right ear and iqamah in the left for protection from Umm al-Sibyan. > **""Whoever has a child born to him, then calls the adhan in his right ear and the iqamah in his left ear, Umm al-Sibyan will not harm him.""**"
"6207","Abu Rafi' (رضي الله عنه) reported that the Prophet ﷺ called the adhan in the ears of al-Hasan and al-Husayn (رضي الله عنهما) when they were born and commanded it."
"6208","Al-Hasan (رحمه الله) reported that Uthman ibn Abi al-'As (رضي الله عنه) was invited to a circumcision feast and refused to attend, explaining the practice in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."
"6209","In another wording Uthman (رضي الله عنه) was invited to food and told it was for a girl's circumcision, whereupon he declared it unseen in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and refused to eat."
